
Gateway reliability host tests
==============================

Run the fixed-frame shots mapping regression test with:

  node "C:\TipIn\TipIn Gateway\test\scoreboard_shots_test.js"

It reads the production C++ field offsets and applies its digit-filtering
semantics to the captured 110-versus-10 frame, adjacent-field variations,
single/two-digit shots, and blank-shot fallback. It is a host mapping test,
not execution of the ESP32 C++ parser; also build the firmware and verify the
physical feed after deployment.

gateway_reliability_test.cpp is a standalone C++11 assertion-based test executable.
It requires no ESP32, network connection or additional test framework.

From a Visual Studio Developer Command Prompt, compile and run (use a scratch
directory for the executable and object file):

  cl /nologo /EHsc /I "C:\TipIn\TipIn Gateway\include" "C:\TipIn\TipIn Gateway\test\gateway_reliability_test.cpp" /Fe:gateway_reliability_test.exe
  gateway_reliability_test.exe

The tests cover the 20-IP history, eight active WebSocket limit, combined HTTP/WS
deduplication, repeated admin reconnects, independent same-IP session health,
recent/inactive boundary, live-IP-safe eviction, matching
pong-only liveness, authentication/pong/congestion deadlines, Wi-Fi escalation
boundaries, suppression during configuration tests, restored connections, and
32-bit millis rollover. They do not prove physical Wi-Fi or async socket recovery.

gateway_clients_json_test.cpp additionally tests the actual API serializer with
ArduinoJson (restored by the normal firmware build). From the same scratch folder:

  cl /nologo /EHsc /I "C:\TipIn\TipIn Gateway\include" /I "C:\TipIn\TipIn Gateway\.pio\libdeps\esp32dev\ArduinoJson\src" "C:\TipIn\TipIn Gateway\test\gateway_clients_json_test.cpp" /Fe:gateway_clients_json_test.exe
  gateway_clients_json_test.exe

It verifies exact top-level/record keys, nullable ages, connection states,
credential exclusion, escaped viewer names, and wrap-safe age output.
They also verify mixed-transport IP rows, deduplicated client names, active session
counts, oldest-open-session duration, and latest activity basis.

Run the IP grouping UI mock test with:

  node "C:\TipIn\TipIn Gateway\test\gateway_clients_ui_test.js"

After a firmware build, firmware_info_test.cpp verifies the actual generated
metadata and additive JSON fields. Compile like gateway_clients_json_test.cpp,
also passing /I "C:\TipIn\TipIn Gateway\.pio\build\esp32dev\generated".
Run the matching admin UI mock test with:

  node "C:\TipIn\TipIn Gateway\test\firmware_info_ui_test.js"

Build firmware and the admin filesystem without uploading:

  platformio run
  platformio run --target buildfs

After an explicitly approved hardware deployment, verify authenticated and
unauthenticated requests to /api/clients, a normal viewer's matching pongs,
viewer reconnects, and an isolated test access point outage. Verify reconnect
attempts at 10 seconds, radio reinitialization at 60 seconds, and a setup AP
after 120 seconds (30 seconds on boot), with scoreboard operation continuing.
Run a multi-hour soak with the tablet and admin page, recording heap minima,
disconnect reasons, reconnect/reinitialize counts, and skipped frames. A build
and host tests alone cannot establish that the previously observed outage is fixed.
